From eea89554f20fd732dc75001174eec97b6876c120 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 5656565566 <contact@home56.top>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 20:06:07 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] init: keep Floral IPC private before cloning mount namespaces

SetupMountNamespaces recursively makes the root shared. Restore the
per-generation Floral IPC leaf to private before bootstrap/default
namespaces diverge, rather than relying on a later early-init action.

Require a single existing safe mount, pin its no-follow directory FD,
check mount identity before and after the propagation change, and reject
unexpected flags, propagation, submounts, owners and modes. Do not create
a fallback transport when the optional container mount is absent.

Keep Android root propagation unchanged and cover the mountinfo checks
with init unit tests. Host validation also exercises the actual helper
in disposable mount/PID namespaces; Android product/board acceptance is
still required.
---
 init/Android.bp                |   1 +
 init/floral_ipc_mount.h        | 165 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 init/floral_ipc_mount_test.cpp |  58 ++++++++++++
 init/mount_namespace.cpp       |   9 ++
 4 files changed, 233 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 init/floral_ipc_mount.h
 create mode 100644 init/floral_ipc_mount_test.cpp

diff --git a/init/Android.bp b/init/Android.bp
index fd4c75f..d940021 100644
--- a/init/Android.bp
+++ b/init/Android.bp
@@ -392,6 +392,7 @@ cc_test {
         "epoll_test.cpp",
         "firmware_handler_test.cpp",
         "floral_device_profile_test.cpp",
+        "floral_ipc_mount_test.cpp",
